  "strongest_supported_science_claim": "For the entire prospectively frozen R0 finite sublanguage of 18,432 distinct descriptors and 73,728 boundary-point executions, an independently specified W9 reference whose exact expected-trace root was frozen before any R0 W7/W8 comparison matched W7 direct execution, W8 direct execution, both bidirectional crossed replays, and independent W5/W6 reconstruction on both producer paths with zero discrepancies. Four deliberately mistranslated compiled profiles remained internally self-consistent across W7, W8, crossed replay, W5, and W6 but were all vetoed by W9; one effect-order mutation and one predicate mutation even preserved the K1 REALIZE set, demonstrating that the orthogonal reference lane detects refinement errors invisible to ordinary differential agreement and, in those controls, to the explicit K1 set projection.",
